---
# Battery Design Plan — t1_r1_noforce (next-generation pure-electric-sedan cell)

## 1. Objective decomposition (parsed from task text, thresholds verbatim)
- stage2 (cell performance): gravimetric energy density ≥ 392.61 Wh/kg (contract caliber: stack dry mass, electrolyte excluded — bda calc-energy).
- stage3 (safety): 4C fast charge with no lithium plating (anode surface potential never < 0 V); max cell temperature ≤ 60 °C (= 333.15 K) during 4C charge at 45 °C ambient; overcharge to 4.7 V must not trigger thermal runaway (run-tr triggered=false).

Multi-objective tension (expected trade-off directions):
- ED ↑ needs thicker/denser electrodes, thin collectors+separator → worsens 4C plating (longer Li⁺ transport paths, higher anode utilization) and raises T_max (more I²R + less surface/volume).
- Plating ↓ needs thin electrodes/small particles/high-σ electrolyte/higher N/P → eats ED.
- T_max ↓ needs cooling h ↑ (thermal DOF) and lower resistance → ED-neutral to mildly negative (porosity).
- Overcharge 4.7 V safety: higher-Ni NMC releases more O2 at high SOC; design mitigants = thermal headroom (T_max budget), cathode stability. Evaluated mechanically (overcharge + run-tr).

## 2. Candidate strategy
- Base system: task names no electrode system → anchor-table default Chen2020 (NMC811/graphite baseline parameterization; overcharge +0.5 V from its 4.2 V cut-off lands exactly on the 4.7 V spec).
- Round 1: baseline characterization — 1C discharge (SPMe→DFN), calc-energy, 4C_charge_45C (lumped+plating), overcharge + run-tr. Establishes the gap to every criterion.
- Opening ceiling assessment (ceiling_escalation ON): probe best-legal architecture+formulation on Chen2020 (thin collectors, thin/high-porosity separator, low-porosity thick electrodes, high-σ electrolyte, N/P tuned, small particles). If ceiling < 392.61 → escalate to Stage 2 material design: system switch to SiOx-bearing OKane2022 (higher anode capacity) or composition/additive candidates.
- Follow-up (exploration_force OFF → free exploration, variants proposed at relevant moments): Pareto walk ED vs plating/T; every candidate that meets stage2 gets full stage3 safety exam; final design gets 1C+4C+overcharge verification.

## 3. Budget allocation
- R1 baseline + R2 ceiling probe: 2 rounds.
- R3–R6: ED-maximization architecture/material iterations (Chen2020 then escalated system).
- R7–R9: safety fine-tuning (plating margin, T_max, overcharge TR margin) + aging sanity check.
- Closing: deliverables + render + verify-deliverables (no true compute: real_compute=false).

## 4. Risk and fallback plan
- ED unreachable on Chen2020 architecture space → escalate (Stage 2): SiOx system switch / high-voltage alternatives (LNMO excluded: its overcharge window mismatches the 4.7 V spec) / composition candidates.
- 4C plating on thick electrodes → negative particle radius ↓, electrolyte σ/t⁺ ↑, N/P ↑, porosity ↑ (accept ED cost).
- T_max > 333.15 K → cooling h ↑ (thermal management DOF) + resistance reduction.
- Three-strike: 3 consecutive same-cause failures → question system/boundary/metric assumptions (record in plan-update + final escalation).
- Chen2020 lacks complete thermal/geometry/plating params → run-pyamm injects defaults (traced in injected_defaults); T_max/plating judgments on Chen2020 marked "approximate (default-injection)" — a reason to prefer a full-parameter system for the final design if escalation occurs.

