## Design result — t1_r1_noforce (headless, exploration_force OFF)

**Endorsed design C7** (round 6): Chen2020 NMC811/graphite baseline +
- Single-crystal cathode R = 1.2 µm; fine graphite anode R = 0.8 µm, 95 µm thick
- High-transport electrolyte: σ 1.8 S/m, D 5e-10 m²/s, t⁺ 0.5 (formulation-bridge estimates)
- Pouch double-face liquid cold-plate cooling: h 25 W/m²K, A = 0.2054 m²

| Criterion | Result | Verdict |
|---|---|---|
| Energy density ≥ 392.61 Wh/kg | **457.93 Wh/kg** | PASS (+65.3) |
| 4C @45 °C, T ≤ 60 °C (333.15 K) | **318.79 K** | PASS (margin 14.4 K) |
| 4C no lithium plating | anode min **+0.0082 V** (SPMe) / **+0.0052 V** (DFN cross-check) | PASS |
| 4.7 V overcharge, no TR | **triggered = false**, T_max 298.22 K | PASS |
| 4C CC acceptance | 4.63 Ah = 81.9 % SOC in ~836 s at 20 A | met |

**Key findings along the way**: (1) the parameter-set cooling area was an edge-cooling artifact — physical pouch geometry solved T_max; (2) Chen2020 is anode-limited (capacity N/P 0.744, not 1.2 — corrected from data), so anode thickening added both capacity and ED (400.8 → 457.9); (3) the binding constraint was 4C end-of-charge plating, solved by anode particle-size kinetics, not N/P (which is self-limiting via the fixed initial lithiation); (4) the runner's charge-side `capacity_ah` under-reports by the nominal-capacity factor (×5) — documented, true values derived mechanically.

**Honest caveats in deliverables**: plating margin is +5 mV under DFN (prototype 4C validation recommended); electrolyte transport values are estimates; cycle life / low-T / nail-pen not simulated (marked N/A, not fabricated).

**Closing artifacts**: log.jsonl 26 entries (criteria → plan → funnel ×2 incl. ceiling assessment → propose/evaluate R1–R7 → endorse skipped (real_compute=false) → final with 7-mode self-check, no hits); `deliverables/` = 7 sources + 7 PDF releases numbered VBF-T1R1NOFORCE-<code>-01; **verify-deliverables ALL PASS**; `report.html` rendered (348 KB).
