**Key findings along the way**: (1) the parameter-set cooling area was an edge-cooling artifact — physical pouch geometry solved T_max; (2) Chen2020 is anode-limited (capacity N/P 0.744, not 1.2 — corrected from data), so anode thickening added both capacity and ED (400.8 → 457.9); (3) the binding constraint was 4C end-of-charge plating, solved by anode particle-size kinetics, not N/P (which is self-limiting via the fixed initial lithiation); (4) the runner's charge-side `capacity_ah` under-reports by the nominal-capacity factor (×5) — documented, true values derived mechanically.

**Honest caveats in deliverables**: plating margin is +5 mV under DFN (prototype 4C validation recommended); electrolyte transport values are estimates; cycle life / low-T / nail-pen not simulated (marked N/A, not fabricated).

